parameters.text:
=You are a mobile app quality analyst triaging an app store review.

Platform: {{ $json.platform }}
App version: {{ $json.appVersion }}
Rating: {{ $json.rating }}
Review text: {{ $json.reviewText }}

Classify this review:
- isTechnicalComplaint: true if the review describes a crash, bug, error message, performance problem, data loss, sync failure, login/auth failure, or other technical malfunction. False for pure praise, feature requests, pricing complaints, or unrelated noise.
- appArea: one of 'crash', 'performance', 'payments', 'sync', 'login_auth', or 'other'
- severity: 'Critical' (crash/data loss/blocks core use), 'High', 'Medium', or 'Low'
- issueSummary: a short, normalized one-sentence description of the underlying technical issue (used later to match duplicates), empty string if not a technical complaint

Return ONLY a JSON object (no markdown fences, no commentary) with keys: isTechnicalComplaint (boolean), appArea, severity, issueSummary, classificationReasoning (one short sentence).

parameters.jsCode:
const upstream = $('Set - Config').first().json;
const response = $input.first().json;

let parsed = {
  isTechnicalComplaint: true,
  appArea: 'other',
  severity: 'Medium',
  issueSummary: upstream.reviewText,
  classificationReasoning: 'AI classification unavailable this cycle; defaulted to treating this as a technical complaint for review.'
};
try {
  const raw = String(response.output || response.text || response.response || '{}').replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();
  const result = JSON.parse(raw);
  parsed = { ...parsed, ...result };
} catch (e) {
  // keep safe default above
}

return [{
  json: {
    ...upstream,
    isTechnicalComplaint: parsed.isTechnicalComplaint,
    appArea: parsed.appArea,
    severity: parsed.severity,
    issueSummary: parsed.issueSummary,
    classificationReasoning: parsed.classificationReasoning
  }
}];

parameters.text:
=You are deduplicating app store complaints.

New review issue summary: {{ $json.issueSummary }}
App area: {{ $json.appArea }} | Platform: {{ $json.platform }} | Version: {{ $json.appVersion }}

Recently logged similar complaints:
{{ JSON.stringify($json.similarComplaints ?? ($json.results || $json.matches || []), null, 2) }}

Decide whether the new review describes the SAME underlying technical issue as an existing cluster above, or a NEW distinct issue.

Return ONLY a JSON object (no markdown fences, no commentary) with keys: isDuplicate (boolean), matchedClusterId (string, the id/reference of the matched complaint cluster if isDuplicate is true, otherwise empty string), clusterReasoning (one short sentence).

parameters.jsCode:
const upstream = $('HTTP - Search Similar Recent Complaints').first().json;
const config = $('JS - Parse Classification Output').first().json;
const response = $input.first().json;

let parsed = {
  isDuplicate: false,
  matchedClusterId: '',
  clusterReasoning: 'AI clustering unavailable this cycle; defaulted to treating this as a new distinct issue.'
};
try {
  const raw = String(response.output || response.text || response.response || '{}').replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();
  const result = JSON.parse(raw);
  parsed = { ...parsed, ...result };
} catch (e) {
  // keep safe default above
}

return [{
  json: {
    ...config,
    similarComplaints: upstream.results || upstream.matches || [],
    isDuplicate: parsed.isDuplicate,
    matchedClusterId: parsed.matchedClusterId,
    clusterReasoning: parsed.clusterReasoning
  }
}];

const upstream = $('JS - Parse Cluster Output').first().json;
const bugResponse = $input.first().json;
const matches = bugResponse.issues || bugResponse.results || bugResponse.matches || [];
const bestMatch = matches.find(m => (m.confidence ?? m.score ?? 0) >= 0.6) || null;

return [{
  json: {
    ...upstream,
    matchedBug: bestMatch,
    hasExistingBugMatch: bestMatch !== null
  }
}];

const item = $input.first().json;
let routingMap = {};
try { routingMap = JSON.parse(item.teamRoutingMapJson || '{}'); } catch (e) { routingMap = {}; }

const routing = routingMap[item.appArea] || { team: 'App Quality', channel: item.engineeringSlackChannelDefault || '#eng-app-quality' };

let resolutionPath = 'new_ticket';
if (item.hasExistingBugMatch === true) {
  resolutionPath = 'bump_existing_bug';
} else if (item.isDuplicate === true) {
  resolutionPath = 'new_ticket';
}

return [{
  json: {
    ...item,
    routingTeam: routing.team,
    routingSlackChannel: routing.channel,
    resolutionPath
  }
}];

